EN:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Thanks for stopping to say hi.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
I must look like a lost tourist, huh.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0026:}}Actually, the opposite is true!
I used to live in this town,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} so I know
where I'm going.

ES:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Gracias por pararte a saludarme.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Seguro que parezco un turista
despistado, ¿eh?{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} {{TAG:0003:0026:}}¡Pues no es así!
Yo antes vivía en este pueblo,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
así que tengo muy claro adónde voy.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Caspitina, che pensiero gentile
fermarsi a salutare.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Devo sembrarti
un turista smarrito, eh?{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0026:}}In realtà hai preso un granchio!
Pensa che una volta io abitavo qui,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
quindi mi oriento benissimo.

DE:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Nett von dir, mal Hallo zu sagen.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Du fragst dich bestimmt, was ein
Fremder wie ich hier macht.
{{TAG:0003:0026:}}Dabei bin ich gar kein Fremder!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Ich hab früher auch mal hier
gewohnt, weißt du.

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Selam vermek için durmana sevindim.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Kaybolmuş turist gibi görünüyorum herhalde.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0026:}}Aslında tam tersi! Eskiden bu kasabada
yaşıyordum,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} yani yolu biliyorum.
